<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg" data-parallax="0.15"><img src="/assets/img/photos/church.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/church-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/church.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="682" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/counties-and-cities/">Counties &amp; cities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Columbus</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">North Mississippi</p><h1>Columbus Claim Appraisal for Historic and Newer Homes</h1><p class="lede">Columbus pairs antebellum homes with Air Force families and a recent EF3 tornado. If the carrier’s estimate on your Columbus property falls short, appraisal can settle the amount.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><ul class="hero-facts"><li><small>County</small><b>Lowndes County</b></li><li><small>Region</small><b>North Mississippi</b></li><li><small>Inspections</small><b>On site</b></li></ul></div></section><div class="wrap cols"><article class="prose"><div class="glance">
<div><p class="glance-h">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><ul class="chips"><li>Downtown Columbus</li><li>Southside</li><li>Caledonia</li><li>New Hope</li><li>Steens</li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Housing mix</p><p>Columbus has antebellum and Victorian homes in its historic districts, mid-century brick ranches, rental housing near the university and the Air Force base, and newer subdivisions in eastern Lowndes County.</p></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Storm history</p><ul class="storm-list"><li><b>Feb 23, 2019</b><span>EF3 tornado through Columbus</span></li><li><b>Feb 2021</b><span>Winter storm and statewide freeze</span></li><li><b>Dec 2022</b><span>Hard freeze and frozen-pipe losses</span></li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips chips-red"><li>Tornadoes and spring severe weather</li><li>Hail and straight-line wind</li><li>Tree fall on large historic lots</li><li>Frozen pipes in older homes</li></ul></div>
</div><h2>Columbus and Lowndes County</h2>
<p>Columbus is the county seat of Lowndes County, on the Tombigbee River near the eastern state line. It is home to Mississippi University for Women and to Columbus Air Force Base, a pilot training base north of the city. Starkville and Mississippi State University are a short drive west.</p>
<p>Columbus is also one of Mississippi’s well-known historic towns. Its spring Pilgrimage opens antebellum and Victorian homes to visitors, and many of those houses are still lived in.</p>

<h2>The February 2019 tornado</h2>
<p>On February 23, 2019, an EF3 tornado moved through Columbus, damaging homes, businesses and trees along its path. Claims from that storm included total losses, roofs torn open, and long fights over interior water damage after rain followed through the openings.</p>
<p>Many of those claims also raised questions about tree removal, fences and outbuildings, and additional living expenses for families who could not stay in their homes during repairs.</p>
<p>Beyond that event, Columbus sees the same severe weather as the rest of North Mississippi: spring storm systems with hail, straight-line wind and tornadoes, plus the occasional hard freeze like the February 2021 winter storm.</p>

<h2>Historic homes and Pilgrimage houses</h2>
<p>Downtown Columbus and the Southside historic district hold many of the city’s antebellum and Victorian homes. Claims on these houses rarely fit a standard estimate.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Common carrier approach</th><th>What a proper repair may need</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Plaster walls and ceilings</td><td>Drywall patch and paint</td><td>Plaster repair by a skilled trade</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wood siding and trim</td><td>Stock lumber</td><td>Custom-milled profiles to match</td></tr>
<tr><td>Heart-pine flooring</td><td>Replace damaged boards only</td><td>Matching reclaimed boards and refinishing a continuous area</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tall windows and doors</td><td>Standard-size replacements</td><td>Restoration or custom units</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Whether a policy pays to match original materials depends on its wording. The cost of repairing covered damage properly is the core question appraisal answers.</p>

<h2>Newer homes, rentals and base housing</h2>
<p>Mid-century brick ranches fill much of the city. Rentals cluster near MUW and serve families stationed at the base. Areas such as Caledonia, New Hope and Steens have newer subdivisions and rural homes. On these properties, the typical disputes are:</p>
<ul>
<li>Partial roof replacements after hail or wind that leave mismatched shingles.</li>
<li>Short roof measurements and missing items like drip edge, starter and ridge.</li>
<li>Tornado-damaged siding replaced on one wall when the color no longer matches.</li>
<li>Tree removal capped by policy limits while the framing repair is underestimated.</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout"><b class="callout-t">Starting point</b><p>Read your carrier’s estimate line by line before you respond. Our <a href="/claim-advice/line-by-line-estimate-reading/">estimate reading guide</a> shows how.</p></div>

<h2>Our work in Columbus</h2>
<p>We work claims across Lowndes County and nearby Starkville. When coverage is accepted and the disagreement is about amount, we can represent you through your policy’s appraisal clause. See our <a href="/our-appraisal-services/tornado-wind-damage-appraisal/">tornado and wind damage appraisal</a> service, and confirm your deadlines with a Mississippi attorney.</p>
<h2>Appraisal services in Columbus</h2>
<p>Every Mississippi Insurance Appraiser service is available in Columbus and the rest of Lowndes County, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Home Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/tornado-wind-damage-appraisal/">Tornado &amp; Wind Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/carrier-estimate-review/">Carrier Estimate Review</a></li></ul>
<h2>Columbus claim questions</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>Can appraisal help with a Pilgrimage home in Columbus?</summary><p>Yes, if the dispute is about the cost to repair covered damage. Historic homes often need specialty trades and materials, and those costs belong in a proper scope of repair.</p></details><details><summary>Do you also work claims in Starkville?</summary><p>Yes. We work claims in Starkville, across Lowndes and Oktibbeha counties, and throughout Mississippi.</p></details></div>
